     ],
     "value": "Component of a transport protein particle (TRAPP) complex that may function in specific stages of inter-organelle traffic (PubMed:16025134, PubMed:16828797). Specifically involved in the early development of neural circuitry, likely by controlling the frequency and amplitude of intracellular calcium transients implicated in the regulation of neuron differentiation and survival (Probable)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "FUNCTION"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
